      {
        "bug_id": "BUG-002",
        "title": "INTEGER_UNDERFLOW_IN_EDIT_COOKIE_SIZE_CALCULATION",
        "root_cause": {
          "type": "Integer Underflow",
          "description": "In edit_cookie, the read size for editing a cookie is computed as msg_size[index] - 1. The msg_size[index] value is a 32-bit int read from the msg_size[] array. If msg_size[index] is 0 (which is possible when create_cookie is called with message_length=0, since scanf(\"%lld\") reads 0 and the check 'cmp rax,0x100; jle' allows 0), then 0 - 1 = -1 (0xFFFFFFFF as unsigned int). This value is then sign-extended via 'movsxd rdx, eax' to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, producing an extremely large read() size parameter."
