          "type": "Use-After-Free",
          "description": "In eat_cookie, when the randomly selected index equals cookie_num-1 (the last element), the swap-remove operation performs a self-assignment: free(msg[cookie_num-1]) is called first, then msg[cookie_num-1] = msg[cookie_num-1] (a no-op self-copy), then cookie_num is decremented. The freed pointer remains stored in msg[old_cookie_num-1]. After decrement, this slot is at index cookie_num (the new, decremented value), which is outside the valid range [0, cookie_num-1]. While edit_cookie and read_cookie check index < cookie_num (preventing direct access under normal conditions), the signedness mismatch in BUG-001 can be used to access this out-of-range slot with a negative index, or create_cookie can re-increment cookie_num and overwrite the slot before it is accessed. The UAF is only exploitable in combination with BUG-001 or through careful sequencing of eat/create operations."
